ence stone now  faces for obstruction and witness  tampering nine years for doing something  that nobody even can define what he did  and soon after the Justice Department  headed by Trump's Attorney General Bill  Barr overruled prosecutors and asked for  stone to face less prison time this is  an abuse of power that the president is  again trying to manipulate federal law  enforcement to serve his political  interest for government lawyers have  resigned in protest renewing accusations  that the Attorney General is serving the  interests of Trump and not the American  people I want to thank the Justice  Department for seeing this bar responded  by telling the President to stay out of  it I cannot do my job here at the  department with a constant background  commentary that that undercuts me  I have never obstructed justice in the  decades after Richard Nixon and  Watergate presidents went out of their  way to avoid the slightest perception of  interference in the justice system not  so in the Trump era where the Attorney  General has positioned himself to do the  president's bidding I think we are  saying  mantling of the post-watergate reforms  like nothing we've seen in decades stone  now awaits his lighter sentence and is  holding out hope for a full presidential  pardon the fear in Washington is that  the president learned a lesson after his  impeachment acquittal that he can move  the wheels of justice to protect his  friends and prosecute his enemies with  impunity  Jackson prosecco Global News Washington  still ahead a volcano erupts at the  crack of dawn lighting up the skies in  Mexico  that thunderous boom rang out in Mexico  indicating the Popocatepetl volcano  erupted a webcam capture the night skies  light up as the crater spewed lava and  an ash column nearly 5000 feet high the  volcano is 80 kilometres from Mexico  City and one of the most active in the  country no one was hurt but a volcanic  ash advisory has been issued one of  Antarctica's fastest