e handle this animal now the cause  isn't known it could be transmission  from conservationists or contamination  in a river but antibiotic resistance is  a massive issue a Canadian group raised  alarm bells this past fall it found that  in 2018 in Canada 26% of bacterial  infections were resistant to treatment  but predicted that number could hit 40  percent by 2050 the Rhino study shows  the misuse and overuse of antibiotics by  humans is affecting other species even  in the wild as well Mike Armstrong  Global News that is global national for  this Thursday I'm Robin Gill tonight  your Canada is dildo Newfoundland and  Labrador we would love to see your part  of this country so email your pictures  to viewers at global national comm thank  you for watching and I'll see you back  here tomorrow have a great night  [Music]
 

